# The @qits scope lives in the platform's own npm repository, not on npmjs. Two lines, and two
# services: everything through qits-platform-mirror's npmjs pull-through cache, ours from
# qits-artifacts' hosted registry. Both are the platform's public hosts; CI writes the in-network
# pair from environment instead, and rewrites the lockfile's origins to match.
#
# Both hosts answer 401 without a credential. Put it in ~/.npmrc, keyed by the scheme-less URL:
#   //mirror.qits.wohlben.eu/npm/npmjs/:_authToken=...
#   //registry.qits.wohlben.eu/artifacts/npm/npm/:_authToken=...
#
# THIS FILE IS .dockerignore'd, DELIBERATELY. npm ranks a project .npmrc ABOVE ~/.npmrc, and the
# image build writes ~/.npmrc from the two build-args the release step hands the builder — so a copy
# of this file inside the build context would silently win and send every request to an address the
# builder cannot resolve. See docker/Dockerfile and app.yml's Dockerfile contract.
registry=https://mirror.qits.wohlben.eu/npm/npmjs/
@qits:registry=https://registry.qits.wohlben.eu/artifacts/npm/npm/
